  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"At rehearsal’s end, the conductor can identify a small amount of optional home practice, using the same scores and approved recordings already available.\", \"decision\": \"How should the choir agree what to practice before next time?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nSection leaders propose one practice priority for their parts, and the conductor confirms these before the notes are sent. Home preparation targets distinct section needs while remaining consistent with the musical direction for the whole choir.\nThe conductor names two practice priorities at the end and includes the relevant bars in the rehearsal notes. Singers leave with a limited, specific task that can be found again without remembering an extended spoken explanation.\nSingers choose a passage they found difficult from a conductor-approved list and record it as their personal practice priority. Preparation follows individual uncertainty while staying within the material the conductor considers useful for the next rehearsal."
    }
  ],
